window.docContents[96].resolve({"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Mm.Mremap/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Mm___Mremap":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Mm › Mremap.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the symbolic proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 91 of 126 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nLinux Virtual Memory mremap SyscallTrusted model of the Linux AArch64 mremap syscall (mm/mremap.c, include/uapi/linux/mman.h), defining Memory.remapRw, SYS_MREMAP, MREMAP_MAYMOVE, and execMremap.\n\n\n\ndef remapRwL29–54 ↗#Move or resize a non-frozen Perm.rw range [oldBase, oldBase + oldSize) onto [newBase, newBase + newSize):* frozen bytes ((m.perm a).frozen) are unconditionally preserved;* for any non-frozen byte a in [newBase, newBase + newSize) at offset off := (a - newBase).toNat, maps some (some p, b) where for off < oldSize (src := oldBase + off) b = m.read8 src and p = { Perm.rw with lazyFree := m.isLazyFree src, anon := m.isAnon src }, and for off ≥ oldSize b = 0#8 and p = Perm.rw;* for any remaining non-frozen byte a in [oldBase, oldBase + oldSize), unmaps (none);* all other bytes keep m.cells a.\n\n\n\ndef SYS_MREMAPL58–60 ↗#Linux AArch64 mremap syscall number (__NR_mremap = 216, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:597, mm/mremap.c:1964).\n\ndef MREMAP_MAYMOVEL62–63 ↗#mremap flags bit MREMAP_MAYMOVE (1, include/uapi/linux/mman.h:8).\n\ndef execMremapL65–124 ↗#mremap(old_address, old_size, new_size, flags) (__NR_mremap = 216, SYSCALL_DEFINE5(mremap) and vma_to_resize / move_vma in mm/mremap.c:1964), modeled for flags == MREMAP_MAYMOVE (1) on a single mapped Perm.rw anonymous range:* [INTENTIONAL_SCOPE]: any flags ≠ MREMAP_MAYMOVE fails closed with .Exception \"unmodeled mremap flags\";* old_address (X0) not page-aligned, new_size == 0 (X2 == 0), or 64-bit PAGE_ALIGN overflow on new_size (newLen > 2 ^ 64 - PAGE_SIZE) returns -EINVAL (offset_in_page and !PAGE_ALIGN(new_len) in mm/mremap.c:1819 check_mremap_params);* old_size == 0 (X1 == 0) fails closed with .Exception \"unmodeled mremap (old_size == 0)\";* with oldAligned := pageAlignUp oldLen and newAligned := pageAlignUp newLen:* if oldAddr.toNat + oldAligned > USER_VA_LIMIT, returns -EINVAL;* if [oldAddr, oldAddr + oldAligned) intersects any frozen byte, fails closed with .Exception \"mremap on frozen memory\";* if [oldAddr, oldAddr + oldAligned) is completely unmapped (s.mem.canMap oldAddr oldAligned), returns -EFAULT (vma_lookup miss in vma_to_resize, mm/mremap.c:1110);* if [oldAddr, oldAddr + oldAligned) is not uniformly some Perm.rw, fails closed with .Exception \"unmodeled mremap (range not uniformly PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE)\";* otherwise queries s.oracleIdx ([INTENTIONAL_OVERAPPROX]):* if s.oracle.mremapFail s.oracleIdx is true, consumes the oracle query (s.nextOracle), leaves s.mem unchanged, and returns -ENOMEM;* otherwise computes mUnmapped := s.mem.unmapNonFrozen oldAddr oldAligned and sanitizes s.oracle.mmap s.oracleIdx via sanitizeMmapAddr mUnmapped cand newAligned.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Mm/Mremap.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Mm.Mremap/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Mm___Mremap"}});